Hello community!
In discovering the ACAD SDK and Tapir Docs, I realized that we can use `ACAPI_Window_ChangeWindow` to jump to a specific databaseId by constructing  (e.g. drawing). It could be interesting for some use-cases.
My proposal for a implementation:
```cpp

GS::ObjectState ChangeWindowCommand::Execute (const GS::ObjectState& parameters, GS::ProcessControl& /*processControl*/) const
{

    // extension
    GS::UniString databaseIdStr;
    // if there is any databaseId parameter, we will try to find it and jump to that window.
    // in that case, the windowType parameter will be ignored if it is provided.
    // if there is no databseId parameter, we fall back to the required windowType parameter.
    if (parameters.Get ("databaseId", databaseIdStr)) {
        const API_Guid databaseId = APIGuidFromString (databaseIdStr.ToCStr ());
        API_DatabaseInfo dbInfo = DatabaseIdResolver::Instance ().GetDatabaseWithId (databaseId);
        const GSErrCode dbErr = ACAPI_Window_GetDatabaseInfo (&dbInfo);
        if (dbErr != NoError) {
            return CreateErrorResponse (dbErr, "Failed to find a database with the given databaseId.");
        }
        API_WindowInfo windowInfo = {};
        windowInfo.typeID = dbInfo.typeID;
        windowInfo.databaseUnId = dbInfo.databaseUnId;
        const GSErrCode err = ACAPI_Window_ChangeWindow (&windowInfo);
        return err == NoError
            ? CreateSuccessfulExecutionResult ()
            : CreateErrorResponse (err, "Failed to change the window to the given database.");
    }

    // existing
    GS::UniString windowTypeStr;
    if (!parameters.Get ("windowType", windowTypeStr)) {
        return CreateFailedExecutionResult (APIERR_BADPARS, "Missing parameter: either windowType or databaseId is required.");
    }

    API_WindowInfo windowInfo = {};
    windowInfo.typeID = ConvertStringToWindowType (windowTypeStr);
    GSErrCode err = ACAPI_Window_ChangeWindow (&windowInfo);
    return err == NoError
        ? CreateSuccessfulExecutionResult ()
        : CreateErrorResponse (err, "Failed to change the window!");
}
```
the extension in the Input scheme:
```cpp
GS::Optional<GS::UniString> ChangeWindowCommand::GetInputParametersSchema () const
{
    return R"({
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
            "windowType": {
                "$ref": "#/WindowType",
                "description": "The type of the window to switch to (FloorPlan, 3DModel, etc.). Ignored when databaseId is provided."
            },
            "databaseId": {
                "$ref":"#/DatabaseId",
                "description": "GUID of a specific database to open (as returned by GetContainingDatabase). Takes precedence over windowType."
            }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false
    })";
}
```
If you think the extension would be useful, I can create a pull request.
Greetings,
