ArchiCAD Build: 28.4.0 (7006) AUS
Tapir Version: 1.5.1
CreateSlabs version:1.0.3

CreateSlabs command crashes ArchiCAD every time when executed. Tested with a simple geometry from terminal command line which could reproduce the crash as well.

Sample test script executed from terminal:
```
curl -sS -X POST http://localhost:19723 \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "command": "API.ExecuteAddOnCommand",
    "parameters": {
      "addOnCommandId": {
        "commandNamespace": "TapirCommand",
        "commandName": "CreateSlabs"
      },
      "addOnCommandParameters": {
        "slabsData": [
          {
            "level": 0,
            "polygonCoordinates": [
              {"x": 0, "y": 0},
              {"x": 5, "y": 0},
              {"x": 5, "y": 5},
              {"x": 0, "y": 5}
            ],
            "polygonArcs": [],
            "holes": []
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }'
```

Not sue if the crash report helps, but I have attached a redacted copy anyway. 
[Archicad-2026-06-12-144111.redacted.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28944299/Archicad-2026-06-12-144111.redacted.txt)

## Environment
- Archicad version: 27
- Tapir Add-On version: latest available as of July 2026 (installed from TapirAddOn_AC27_Mac.bundle, downloaded from the official releases page)
- OS: macOS
- Access method: JSON API command CreateRoofs (also tested via the tapir-archicad-MCP bridge, command elements_create_roofs)

## Summary
The CreateRoofs command unconditionally fails with the error:

Multi-plane roof creation is not yet supported (incomplete pivot-edge plane setup)

This happens regardless of polygon shape, number of levels, presence/absence of eavesOverhang, thickness, or buildingMaterialId. I could not find any parameter combination that succeeds.

## Steps to Reproduce

### Test 1 — Rectangle, single uniform level (intended as hip roof)
{
  "roofsData": [{
    "level": 4,
    "levels": [{ "levelAngle": 0.6109, "levelHeight": 0 }],
    "polygonCoordinates": [
      {"x": 0, "y": 0}, {"x": 20, "y": 0}, {"x": 20, "y": 10}, {"x": 0, "y": 10}
    ],
    "thickness": 0.3
  }]
}

### Test 2 — Rectangle, one level per edge (4 levels)
{
  "roofsData": [{
    "level": 4,
    "levels": [
      {"levelAngle": 0.5236, "levelHeight": 0},
      {"levelAngle": 0.5236, "levelHeight": 0},
      {"levelAngle": 0.5236, "levelHeight": 0},
      {"levelAngle": 0.5236, "levelHeight": 0}
    ],
    "polygonCoordinates": [
      {"x": 0, "y": 0}, {"x": 20, "y": 0}, {"x": 20, "y": 10}, {"x": 0, "y": 10}
    ],
    "thickness": 0.3
  }]
}

### Test 3 — Rectangle with eavesOverhang, no explicit thickness
{
  "roofsData": [{
    "eavesOverhang": 0.6,
    "level": 3,
    "levels": [{ "levelAngle": 0.6109, "levelHeight": 0 }],
    "polygonCoordinates": [
      {"x": -0.6, "y": -0.6}, {"x": 20.6, "y": -0.6}, {"x": 20.6, "y": 5}, {"x": -0.6, "y": 5}
    ],
    "thickness": 0.05
  }]
}

### Test 4 — Minimal triangle (3-point polygon, no hips/valleys possible)
{
  "roofsData": [{
    "level": 3,
    "levels": [{ "levelAngle": 0.6109, "levelHeight": 0 }],
    "polygonCoordinates": [
      {"x": 0, "y": 0}, {"x": 4, "y": 0}, {"x": 2, "y": 4}
    ]
  }]
}

All four tests above return the identical error message. Test 4 is notable: a 3-point polygon with a single uniform pitch is the simplest possible multi-plane roof case (a pyramid hip with no internal valleys), and it still fails — suggesting the feature may not be functionally implemented at all yet, rather than failing only on complex pivot-line geometry.

## Expected Behavior
At least one of the above (particularly Test 4, the simplest possible case) should successfully create a Roof element.

## Actual Behavior
Archicad rejected CreateRoofs: Multi-plane roof creation is not yet supported (incomplete pivot-edge plane setup)
returned every time, with no variation based on input.

## Impact
Users cannot create native Roof elements via the API at all currently (only single-flat-plane workarounds via Slab, or non-classified sloped surfaces via Mesh, are possible — neither of which is correctly categorized as "Roof" in schedules/BOQs or drawing sets, which is the entire point of using the native tool).

## Suggested Fix / Ask
- If this is a known WIP limitation, it would help to state so explicitly in the command's error message or in the docs for CreateRoofs, so users don't spend time debugging parameters.
- If possible, prioritize at least the simplest case (single-pitch / uniform-pitch polygon, Test 1/4 above) since that would unblock the most common residential use case (gable/hip roofs on a rectangular footprint).

## Additional context
ModifyRoofs was also tested against roofs (none exist to modify, since none can be created) — assumed to share the same underlying limitation but not separately confirmed.

Happy to provide the full project file or further reproduction data if useful.

## Summary

`CreateLayerCombinations` accepts per-layer `isHidden`, `isLocked`, `isWireframe`, and `intersectionGroupNr`, but **the per-layer stats are silently ignored** on both create and modify: the layer combination's *name* and *layer membership* are saved, yet every per-layer stat comes back as its default (visible, unlocked, not wireframe, intersection group 1).

## Environment

- Tapir **1.5.7** (latest release, commit `986c6e2`)
- Archicad **27.0.0 R1 (build 3001)**, Windows
- JSON API on `127.0.0.1:19723`

## Repro

Call `CreateLayerCombinations` with one layer forced hidden/locked/wireframe/group 7:

```json
{
  "command": "API.ExecuteAddOnCommand",
  "parameters": {
    "addOnCommandId": { "commandNamespace": "TapirCommand", "commandName": "CreateLayerCombinations" },
    "addOnCommandParameters": {
      "layerCombinationDataArray": [
        {
          "name": "FLAG_TEST",
          "layers": [
            {
              "attributeId": { "guid": "<any real layer GUID>" },
              "isHidden": true,
              "isLocked": true,
              "isWireframe": true,
              "intersectionGroupNr": 7
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "overwriteExisting": false
    }
  }
}
```

Response: `{"attributeIds": [{"attributeId": {"guid": "..."}}]}` — success.

Then `GetLayerCombinations` on the new combination returns the layer with:

```json
{
  "attributeId": { "guid": "<same layer GUID>" },
  "intersectionGroupNr": 1,
  "isHidden": false,
  "isLocked": false,
  "isWireframe": false
}
```

i.e. the requested stats (`true/true/true/7`) are **not applied**.

Same result on **modify** (`overwriteExisting: true` + `attributeId` of an existing combination, sending the full `layers` array echoed from `GetLayerCombinations` with one layer's flags changed), and with both the bare `attributeId: {"guid": ...}` and wrapped `attributeId: {"attributeId": {"guid": ...}}` shapes.

## Expected

Per-layer flags should persist on the layer combination, exactly as they do when the same flags are set through Archicad's Layer Combinations dialog.

## What works (for comparison)

- Renaming an existing combination via `overwriteExisting: true` + `attributeId` ✔
- Layer membership (which layers appear in the combination) ✔
- **Layer-level flags via `CreateLayers`** (`isHidden`/`isLocked`/`isWireframe`/`intersectionGroupNr` on a layer, which affect the currently active combination) ✔ — verified live, applied and read back correctly.

So the drop happens specifically in the layer-combination stat path.

## Possible root cause

In `CreateLayerCombinationsCommand::SetTypeSpecificParameters` (AttributeCommands.cpp):

```cpp
attribute.layerComb.lNumb = layers.GetSize ();
attributeDef.layer_statItems = new GS::HashTable<API_AttributeIndex, API_LayerStat> ();
...
for (const GS::ObjectState& layer : layers) {
    ... build layerStat from isHidden/isLocked/isWireframe/intersectionGroupNr ...
    if (GetAttributeIndexFromAttributeId (layer, API_LayerID, layerIndex)) {
        attributeDef.layer_statItems->Add (layerIndex, layerStat);
    }
}
```

`lNumb` is set to **the number of layers listed in the payload**, but the AC27 devkit (`APIdefs_Attributes.h`, `API_LayerCombType`) documents that `lNumb` "**has the same value in all layer combinations**" (it equals the project's total layer count) and that new layers are auto-added to every combination as visible+unlocked. Passing a partial stat table (only the layers in the payload, e.g. 1 of 60) appears to make Archicad fall back to defaults for the combination rather than applying the supplied stats. A fix may need to seed the stat table from the existing combination (or all project layers) before overriding the listed ones — similar to how `CreatePenTables`/`CreateProfiles` already seed from a source attribute.

## Suggested fix area

`CreateLayerCombinationsCommand::SetTypeSpecificParameters` — seed `layer_statItems` from the existing/template combination (or enumerate all project layers via `ACAPI_Attribute_GetAttributesByType(API_LayerID, ...)`), then apply the caller's overrides on top, keeping `lNumb` consistent with the project's layer count.
